只输出严格JSON，恰好包含id（metadata.id原样）、summary_zh（15到140个Unicode字符，通常40到100字）、category（枚举）、tags（2到5个不重复关键词，每个最多30字符）、confidence（0到1，仅自评）、insufficient_evidence（布尔）、evidence（1到3个对象，每个恰好包含paragraph_id、fact）、limitations（0到5个字符串）。只选择输入中长度20至120字符的完整片段编号；fact是该片段支持的中文事实转述。不要输出quote，不要自行抄写、拼接、删改或补造引用。程序会按编号附上原文。一个编号只用一次；最多3条证据。不得增加字段。
摘要和limitations保留会改变功能意义的前提、平台例外和限制：设密码后才认证、页面保持打开才提醒、依赖外部组件、估算不等于保证。只写已实现功能，不将规划当完成。证据不足就标记，不编造。
图像识别/分类不是媒体创作，没有贴切类别归other；量化、计算与领域研究归search-research，不因多智能体实现归agents-automation；模型/CLI适配与插件开发工具归coding-development；市场/精选目录按搜索发现归search-research。不要按附属同步、备份或评论功能分类。不要推断本机客户端等于本地模型。
摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"Compiler-style pre-execution safety analysis for Harness shell actions.","id":"gh:1317022895","install_available":false,"language":"Rust","name":"Caushell","slug":"fatmo666/Caushell","topics":["ai-agent","bash","claude-code","claude-code-plugin","codex","codex-plugin","deepseek-harness","dsh-plugin","guardrails","hooks","pre-execution","rust","security","semantic-analysis","shell","shell-security","static-analysis"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"Compiler-style pre-execution safety analysis for Harness shell actions."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"Compiler-style pre-execution safety analysis for Harness shell actions."},{"id":"p3s1","text":"English | 简体中文"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"Quick start ·\nConfiguration ·\nWhat Caushell catches ·\nWorking with sandboxes ·\nHow it works"},{"id":"p5s1","text":"Caushell (causal + shell) runs between a Harness and the local shell. Before a shell action reaches "},{"id":"p5s2","text":"the local shell, Caushell performs pre-execution semantic analysis."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"`Shell action → AST → command modeling → session execution graph → safety analysis → decision`"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"It preserves command structure, data flow and state changes across commands, and context such as pat"},{"id":"p7s2","text":"hs, variables, working directory, and Git state. It also emits reviewable structured evidence for de"},{"id":"p7s3","text":"bugging, policy extension, and audit."},{"id":"p8s1","text":"## What Caushell catches"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"Caushell decides based on the actual impact a shell action can have on the local environment. It cov"},{"id":"p9s2","text":"ers common risk classes such as:"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"- Blocking catastrophic deletion or overwrite of critical targets such as system directories, disks,"},{"id":"p10s2","text":" and partitions\n- Requiring approval when remote content flows into a shell or interpreter\n- Recogni"},{"id":"p10s3","text":"zing dangerous shell actions generated under the influence of untrusted context\n- Requiring approval"},{"id":"p10s4","text":" for operations that can destroy the Git worktree, index, branches, or stash\n- Recognizing the actua"},{"id":"p10s5","text":"l impact of variable expansion, globbing, redirection, pipelines, and working directory changes"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"The examples below show the default policy. Each check produces exactly one final decision."},{"id":"p12s1","text":"| Risk | Harness shell action | Default decision |"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"| Normal inspection command | `ls src` | `Allow` |\n| File mutation outside the workspace | `rm /tmp/"},{"id":"p13s2","text":"other/file` | `NeedApproval` |\n| Remote content execution | `curl https://example.com/install.sh \\| "},{"id":"p13s3","text":"bash` | `NeedApproval` |\n| Git local state discard | `git reset --hard HEAD~1` | `NeedApproval` |\n| "},{"id":"p13s4","text":"Git untracked file deletion | `git clean -fdx` | `NeedApproval` |\n| Relative path delete after `cd /"},{"id":"p13s5","text":"` | `cd / && rm -rf etc` | `Deny` |\n| System path deletion | `rm -rf /etc/*` | `Deny` |\n| Disk / par"},{"id":"p13s6","text":"tition overwrite | `sudo dd if=image.iso of=/dev/sda` | `Deny` |"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"## Working with sandboxes"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"Caushell handles pre-execution analysis, while a sandbox enforces runtime restrictions. They can be "},{"id":"p15s2","text":"es pre-execution analysis, while a sandbox enforces runtime restrictions. They can be used together."},{"id":"p16s1","text":"### 1. Protecting workspace and Git state"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"Development workflows usually require a sandbox to allow workspace reads and writes as well as Git c"},{"id":"p17s2","text":"ommands. Under this configuration, `git reset --hard` can still discard local work; Caushell can req"},{"id":"p17s3","text":"uire confirmation or block the action before execution."},{"id":"p18s1","text":"### 2. Identifying file use and data flow"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"A sandbox can control file read and write permissions, but the risk of a file also depends on how it"},{"id":"p19s2","text":" is used. The same read or write creates different risk relationships when it involves a normal proj"},{"id":"p19s3","text":"ect file, remotely downloaded content, input from outside the workspace, startup configuration, or s"},{"id":"p19s4","text":"ensitive configuration. Whether the content flows to the network also affects the decision."},{"id":"p20s1","text":"Tests or local runs may need to read `.env`, while dependency installation or API calls also require"},{"id":"p20s2","text":" network access. Reading sensitive configuration and sending its contents to a remote endpoint forms"},{"id":"p20s3","text":" an exfiltration chain; Caushell can use taint analysis to identify these shell-visible data flows."},{"id":"p21s1","text":"### 3. Making decisions before the process starts"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"Runtime sandboxing blocks a process after it starts and reaches a restricted boundary. Caushell retu"},{"id":"p22s2","text":"rns a decision before the shell action executes."},{"id":"p23s1","text":"For a combined command, pre-execution analysis can identify a later high-risk operation before the e"},{"id":"p23s2","text":"ntire action starts, avoiding the execution of earlier commands. It can also require confirmation or"},{"id":"p23s3","text":" block the action before the process produces side effects."},{"id":"p24s1","text":"## Quick start"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"Install the Caushell runtime:"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"Stable releases are published from `v*` tags. The installer downloads the latest stable GitHub relea"},{"id":"p27s2","text":"se by default. To pin a version, set `CAUSHELL_VERSION`, for example `CAUSHELL_VERSION=v0.0.9`."},{"id":"p28s1","text":"Prebuilt releases support Linux x86_64 as a static binary, macOS x86_64, and Apple Silicon. Windows "},{"id":"p28s2","text":"and Linux ARM64 do not have prebuilt packages yet."},{"id":"p29s1","text":"Then install the corresponding Harness integration. In Codex and Claude Code, these integrations are"},{"id":"p29s2","text":" installed as plugins."},{"id":"p30s1","text":"### Codex"},{"id":"p31s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p32s1","text":"Check the installation:"},{"id":"p33s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p34s1","text":"This checks the installed binaries, hook wrapper, runtime/config compatibility, and daemon state. `r"},{"id":"p34s2","text":"untime daemon is down` is only a warning before the first Harness shell action."},{"id":"p35s1","text":"To verify the Codex integration more deeply, run:"},{"id":"p36s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p37s1","text":"The smoke test checks that Codex sees the enabled `caushell-codex` plugin, then sends harmless synth"},{"id":"p37s2","text":"etic `PreToolUse` and `PostToolUse` hook events through the installed Caushell hook. The success sig"},{"id":"p37s3","text":"nal is `Result: OK`."},{"id":"p38s1","text":"For normal Codex use, review and trust the Caushell hook in `/hooks` if Codex asks you to do so."},{"id":"p39s1","text":"Codex hooks currently cannot ask for approval directly. When Caushell classifies a shell action as `"},{"id":"p39s2","text":"NeedApproval`, the Codex integration blocks it by default and prints the reason. To let Codex run `N"},{"id":"p39s3","text":"eedApproval` actions while still recording Caushell decisions, switch the Codex mode to `observe`:"},{"id":"p40s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p41s1","text":"`Deny` decisions are always blocked."},{"id":"p42s1","text":"### DeepSeek Harness"},{"id":"p43s1","text":"Install the integration into each DSH profile you use:"},{"id":"p44s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p45s1","text":"Persistent Bash is not supported. See the [DeepSeek Harness\nintegration](integrations/deepseek-harne"},{"id":"p45s2","text":"ss/README.md) for source installation\nand configuration."},{"id":"p46s1","text":"### Update an existing installation"},{"id":"p47s1","text":"After the first installation, update Caushell with one command:"},{"id":"p48s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p49s1","text":"[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p50s1","text":"## How it works"},{"id":"p51s1","text":"- How Caushell works: the complete flow from a Harness shell action to the final decision\n- Semantic"},{"id":"p51s2","text":" model: Shell AST, command modeling, variable resolution, and the session execution graph\n- Security"},{"id":"p51s3","text":" model: risk analysis, Decision Assembly, and the Harness execution boundary"}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
